  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="951981b4-81e5-5ab2-b60a-3bac6ae81995" activityNameId="93e44059-749e-5d50-850a-434c8138823d" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Preservative treatment, infrastructure</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Preservative treatment, infrastructure
The plant has a yearly throughput of 6'000 m3 timber, a life time of 50 years (machines are replaced once in this time) and a life time output of 3E5 m3 treated timber. This data must only be used to consider the infrastructure needed for preservative treatment of wood if this is not relevant.;
UUID: 00c8fa8c-74fb-3f8b-a646-4c7a22c79de5
The land area and the material (production and disposal) and their transports needed for a preservative treatment plant is included. Land used for the storing of incoming wood is not included because most preservative treatment is done in the sawmills. The space used for drying after the treatment is included.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Infrastructure for pressurised impregnation. Dip treatment would require less steel but about the same land use.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: estimation 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_00c8fa8c-74fb-3f8b-a646-4c7a22c79de5.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
